            <ArticleTitle>Primitive neuroectodermal tumor/ewing sarcoma presenting with pulmonary nodular lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>957239</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2015/957239</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primitive neuroectodermal tumors (PNETs) and Ewing sarcoma (EWS) belong to the same family of malignant, small, round cell neoplasms of soft tissue or bone origin. EWS-PNETs that arise in the lung parenchyma involvement are extremely rare in adults. A case of a 32-year-old male presenting with chest pain and diffuse pulmonary nodules on chest X-ray and diagnosed with Ewing sarcoma-PNETs will be presented here.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
